<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Bosch GmbH</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1886">1886</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-bosch">Robert Bosch</a> GmbH is a German engineering company founded by Robert Bosch in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> in 1886 as a workshop for precision mechanics and electrical engineering. Its magneto ignition made it a leading supplier to the motor industry, and it became one of the world's largest makers of car parts, tools and household appliances. It is largely owned by a charitable foundation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-bosch-gmbh.jpg" alt="Robert Bosch GmbH" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pjt56 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BoschRenningen-pjt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
